More robust program would use non-transferable and permissioned burn
-> Instead of using non-transferrable extension
-> create transfer hook that prevents transfers when fundraising is on
-> once fundraising settled, clear the transfer hook and permissioned burn making token free to transact
-> Also revoke mint authority to prevent illegal minting in future.
-> Even though contribute path closes mint, upgrade authority of the program can add new instruction that can create new ways to mint and pull the rug
